1
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:12,762
[rocket engine whooshing] 

2
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:16,683
[ominous music playing]

3
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,815
That is the most horrifying thing
I have ever seen.

4
00:00:23,898 --> 00:00:25,650
It's desecrating a sacred object.

5
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:28,570
Agreed. They just trampled over
the American Koran.

6
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:31,489
Isn't that breaking a US law,
even on the moon?

7
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:34,034
US law applies 200 miles from a US flag.

8
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:35,702
Two hundred miles from the coastline.

9
00:00:35,785 --> 00:00:38,121
Now, is the moon 200 miles away?

10
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,957
It is not,
and running over a flag is not illegal.

11
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,208
You're not a lawyer, Naird.

12
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,418
I'm a corporate lawyer.

13
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:46,087
They could argue that we abandoned
that flag when we left the moon.

14
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:47,338
That would make it trash.

15
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,925
Take... that... back.

16
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:52,343
I just meant legally.

17
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,971
Obviously, it's not trash. 
It's the soul of America.

18
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:57,515
We should run over one of their flags,
tit for tat.

19
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:59,726
Where we gonna find a Chinese flag
on the moon?

20
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,519
Make one out of our own?

21
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:06,357
You don't rip up an American flag
to create a Chinese flag, you moron.

22
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:07,817
We need to hit back hard.

23
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:08,735
We can bomb.

24
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:10,403
Big bomb, little bomb.

25
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:11,905
-Smart bomb, stupid bomb.
-[all chuckling] 

26
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,364
There's one for every occasion.

27
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:14,991
A flag is a symbol.

28
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,494
You can't kill people
for insulting a symbol.

29
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:19,037
If it were up to me, we'd invade.

30
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,288
I'm talking some serious

31
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:22,707
-bull-in-a-China shop action.
-[laughing] 

32
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:25,126
Let's knock down the Great Wall
they're so proud of.

33
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,086
We got all these weapons.
We're never allowed to use them.

34
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,046
Drives me crazy.

35
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:30,757
Yeah, I talk to my therapist about this
all the time.

36
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,383
-Where are we at with nukes?
-[laughter]

37
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,927
No, no. We're not going to nuke China.

38
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:36,304
Could we get back on track here
for a second?

39
00:01:36,387 --> 00:01:38,473
Does anyone have
a valid suggestion to make?

40
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,809
We're just joking around, Grandma. Jeez!

41
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:43,561
Yeah, just blowing off steam there.
Don't be such a pussy.

42
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:45,814
Wait. What? No. No, no, no.

43
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:50,151
We need to do one of these ideas,
at least. Maybe more, right? Come on!

44
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:53,404
I mean, aren't you guys tired
of everybody using us like a doormat?

45
00:01:56,199 --> 00:02:00,453
Look, this happened in space,
so the response must be in space as well.

46
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:03,456
-I have consulted a space attorney.
-What the fuck?

47
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,376
-There's no such thing. You got scammed.
-Now who's the dope?

48
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:09,337
We signed
an international outer space treaty.

49
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,923
Any sort of violence
and we break that treaty.

50
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:13,758
We must retaliate. I will handle it.

51
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:14,968
POTUS will be very happy.

52
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:17,428
We will do something
significant and proportionate.

53
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:20,765
I don't think POTUS will be happy
with a proportionate response.

54
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:25,228
Well, then,
it'll be a little more than proportionate.

55
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:27,939
I have taken it upon myself
to have a focus group

56
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:31,484
in which we can determine
what would be an appropriate response.

57
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:34,779
Ideally, what would you like to see happen
on the moon? Anybody.

58
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:39,325
Research that benefits mankind.

59
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:41,578
Yeah. Okay. What about you?
What about you?

60
00:02:41,661 --> 00:02:45,165
Yeah, something that helps everyone
and justifies the cost.

61
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:46,374
Yeah. Yeah. 

62
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:49,002
What would be an example of something bad
that could happen on the moon?

63
00:02:49,085 --> 00:02:50,503
Anybody wanna answer that?

64
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:55,300
An accident where a person gets hurt.

65
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:56,843
[Tony] Yeah, that would be bad, 
wouldn't it?

66
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:59,762
Could you ever imagine
supporting a war on the moon?

67
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:00,763
[laughing] No.

68
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,599
That would be a terrible waste.

69
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:03,600
Really?

70
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:05,768
Do me a favor.
Watch this video real quick.

71
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,482
That's America!
Keep watching. It's not over.

72
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,612
Beep, beep, beep. Crunch.

73
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:17,071
Huh? 

74
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:19,073
Does nobody respect us? Keep looking.

75
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:21,618
That is our country
they're rolling all over.

76
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:24,495
Yeah, we have to do something about that.

77
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:27,832
I mean, maybe not a war,
but we should definitely do something.

78
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:29,876
I'm loving this. Okay, this is fantastic.

79
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:32,795
Let's feel out this direction.
Let's keep it going. Okay, what else?

80
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:35,089
It should be retaliation
on the same level.

81
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:38,134
Like, it should be a prank.
It should be like... graffiti!

82
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,220
Graffiti? All right, keep going.
That's not bad.

83
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,679
Um... ding-dong ditch.

84
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:45,266
Brown paper bag on fire,
but there's poop in it.

85
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:49,437
-I don't know whose poop.
-Right, okay.

86
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,148
-TP their rocket!
-TP their rocket!

87
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,149
I love this.

88
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,108
That's what it takes,

89
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,110
a 100-year-old white man
to make this work!

90
00:03:56,194 --> 00:03:59,030
Okay, let's pop it on the board.
Here we go!

91
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:12,085
[blender whirring] 

92
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,691
How can there be no hammers?

93
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:36,442
We must have packed hammers.

94
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:40,238
No. None of the big doctor brains
packed a hammer.

95
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:43,783
There are wrenches.
Then use a wrench as a hammer.

96
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:46,536
That's not how
you take care of your wrenches!

97
00:04:46,619 --> 00:04:48,997
No toothbrushes or deodorant either,

98
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,166
but there are ten years' worth of tampons,
for some reason.

99
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:55,753
Wait.
Young man, what are you using as a shovel?

100
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,715
Sir, it's actually
Spaceman Obie Hanrahan, sir!

101
00:04:58,798 --> 00:05:00,800
And I'm using a metal moon scoop

102
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:03,594
with an adjustable
crescent-shaped head, sir!

103
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:05,805
-[Eddie] That's a wrench, you dimwit.
-[hissing] 

104
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,849
Hey, what's that hissing noise?

105
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:09,017
Jesus-- Uh...

106
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,562
you have to patch that up immediately,
or you'll all die.

107
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:15,106
The-- The duct tape's in locker 1.

108
00:05:15,189 --> 00:05:18,943
Dr. Mallory, the Chinese Space Agency
just posted some video of their base.

109
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:23,031
-Wow.
-Put it on the big screen.

110
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:26,951
[reporter speaking Mandarin]

111
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,372
How many pillows do you need?

112
00:05:31,456 --> 00:05:33,291
It's already one-sixth gravity.

113
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:36,169
[man] How many did you serve like this?

114
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:39,422
[mockingly]
 "How many did you serve like this?"

115
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:40,965
Are you drunk right now?

116
00:05:41,257 --> 00:05:42,175
[scoffs] 

117
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:44,677
Fine. You're fired.

118
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,179
Should I tell your dad?

119
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,222
You know, sure, dude.

120
00:05:48,681 --> 00:05:49,766
Tell him.

121
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:52,602
He doesn't have a fucking leg to stand on.

122
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:02,236
Okay, this is what I learned,

123
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,030
and I think you're gonna go crazy
for this.

124
00:06:04,113 --> 00:06:06,824
There are three cans of shaving cream
on that moon base,

125
00:06:06,908 --> 00:06:08,451
and there's two cans of hairspray.

126
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:12,121
If we just switch those nozzles,
we can cause some serious mischief.

127
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,415
It's not enough. They trampled our flag.

128
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:15,541
What else you got?

129
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:19,962
Okay, your eyebrows tested poorly
in men and women ages six to 45.

130
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:21,464
Why are you testing my eyebrows?

131
00:06:21,547 --> 00:06:22,423
It was unsolicited.

132
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,050
People just want
to talk about your eyebrows.

133
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:26,010
The joint chiefs are on the phone
in the conference room.

134
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,136
They want an update.

135
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:28,596
[exhaling] 

136
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,473
How's it going, General?

137
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,808
Every news outlet on the planet

138
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:35,019
is showing some Chinese rover
doing donuts on our most sacred...

139
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:36,562
cloth.

140
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:39,107
We need a quick military response.

141
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:40,650
-Oorah!
-Hooah!

142
00:06:40,733 --> 00:06:41,567
-Hooyah!
-Hooyah!

143
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,236
Booyah! 

144
00:06:43,319 --> 00:06:45,446
You have the go-ahead
to attack the Chinese base.

145
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:46,489
How do you wanna do it?

146
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:48,658
Our lead suggestion from the focus group

147
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,743
would be to shaving-cream
the shit out of them.

148
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:52,578
And if that's not enough,

149
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:56,416
we also have the capability to TP as well.

150
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:59,710
And possibly graffiti the side
of their base with "China sucks."

151
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,754
Sound good?

152
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:04,006
-Oora--
-No! No, no, no.

153
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:06,509
We need to burn that Chinese base
to the ground.

154
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:08,469
I thought that's why
you brought an arsonist!

155
00:07:10,263 --> 00:07:13,307
Well, not really, obviously.

156
00:07:13,391 --> 00:07:15,685
Yes, really, obviously!

157
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:19,021
This-- This has been debated
in the policy circles

158
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:21,441
as high up in the administration
as you can think!

159
00:07:21,524 --> 00:07:22,692
It's time to stand tough!

160
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,864
Look, nobody wants to get back
at these commie bastards

161
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:29,407
more than I do, but...

162
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:34,287
breaking a treaty with a reprisal attack
of unwarranted destruction,

163
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:38,499
and putting noncombatant scientists
in harm's way...

164
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,001
Mmm...

165
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:42,420
That's like three violations
of the Geneva Convention.

166
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:43,838
Okay, look.

167
00:07:43,921 --> 00:07:45,715
I'm not a professional politician,

168
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:48,718
but this European International Treaty,
come on!

169
00:07:48,801 --> 00:07:50,303
Don't get captured like a bunch of losers,

170
00:07:50,386 --> 00:07:52,513
and you don't have to worry about
how they treat you.

171
00:07:53,014 --> 00:07:56,184
How about we just continue to look for
some more creative solutions?

172
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:58,436
Yeah, well,
I think destroying the base is lame,

173
00:07:58,519 --> 00:08:02,064
and it's a war crime, uh,
which you should never ever do.

174
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,149
-All right, look!
-Uh, okay.

175
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:04,734
You have your orders, Naird!

176
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:07,111
I need a complete outline and strategy

177
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:09,822
for this battle plan
to destroy this Chinese base,

178
00:08:09,906 --> 00:08:13,159
and I need it shock, I need awe,
and I need it in PDF,

179
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:14,994
'cause my computer doesn't have Word.

180
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:19,624
God.

181
00:08:22,543 --> 00:08:24,629
So that is the order from the top.

182
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:26,839
You can't do that.

183
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:30,635
[stammers]
These are scientists and astronauts.

184
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,595
I have to. It's the chain of command.

185
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:37,516
Mark, they just named the flat area
where we landed The Plains of Mallory.

186
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,561
Oh, that is so cool. Congrats.

187
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:45,483
Thank you. But now, it could become
the site of the first moon atrocity.

188
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,902
I don't want to read that in a textbook.

189
00:08:47,985 --> 00:08:49,487
Yeah, nobody wants that.

190
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,490
I'm sure cooler heads will prevail.

191
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:53,824
Just some saber-rattling.

192
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:58,079
The next resupply
can't launch for a month, so...

193
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:02,833
hopefully, they'll have the time
to cool off before the guns show up.

194
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:05,044
Yeah.

195
00:09:17,682 --> 00:09:19,976
[Mark] Captain Ali,
I'd like you to look in locker 5.

196
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:22,144
It says "spare oxygen."

197
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,145
Just open it.

198
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:33,030
[Obie] Okay, but we do have spare oxygen
somewhere, right?

199
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,450
What do you want us to do with these,
General?

200
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:37,535
I'm not sure yet.

201
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:40,413
Just, uh, show everyone how to use them.

202
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,665
Make sure they're cleaned and loaded.

203
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:44,625
Yes, sir.

204
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:47,795
Loading and cleaning guns.

205
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:52,883
Feels like no matter what I start doing,
I always end up loading and cleaning guns.

206
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:55,803
I haven't been allowed
to touch one of these in forever.

207
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,722
I just hope the general knows
what he's doing.

208
00:09:58,639 --> 00:10:00,141
What if the Chinese have guns?

209
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:03,060
No. They're a research center.

210
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,645
So are we.

211
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:11,152
[Mallory yelling] 
You already have guns on board?

212
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:14,613
No toothbrushes, but room for guns?

213
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:16,449
You lied to me, Naird!

214
00:10:16,532 --> 00:10:18,117
General Naird, Chief Scientist!

215
00:10:18,617 --> 00:10:20,036
They were for self-defense.

216
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:21,370
Oh, sure they were!

217
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:24,999
Sometimes,
provocation requires a show of force!

218
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:28,461
Neville Chamberlain didn't do that,
and Hitler invaded Poland!

219
00:10:28,544 --> 00:10:31,255
Not everything is World War II!

220
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:33,507
Well, not everything is Vietnam!

221
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,093
I thought you were one of the good guys,

222
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:38,554
with your John Wayne swagger.

223
00:10:38,637 --> 00:10:40,514
But you're no John Wayne.

224
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:42,516
You are Wayne John!

225
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,728
-Who?
-Wayne John!

226
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:46,979
Wayne John!

227
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:48,939
I worked with him at IBM!

228
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:50,900
He stole pencils!

229
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:52,360
My pencils!

230
00:10:52,443 --> 00:10:55,404
If you had any integrity at all,
you would quit!

231
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:58,658
The person in line behind me
will be even worse!

232
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:02,536
I know I'm not perfect,
but I know I'm not the worst.

233
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:05,956
Well, you take that up
with your next chief scientist.

234
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,875
-I quit!
-Adrian!

235
00:11:07,958 --> 00:11:08,876
Adrian!

236
00:11:10,294 --> 00:11:11,337
Adrian!

237
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,298
[imitating Rocky] Adrian! Adrian!

238
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:16,717
[imitating Adrian] Rocky! Rocky!

239
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:17,802
Right?

240
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,195
[whispering] Hey, Captain Ali.

241
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:42,535
Whoa. What up, stalker?

242
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:45,704
Just sitting there all creepy, 
staring at me.

243
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,624
How long have you been watching me, huh?

244
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:51,043
Do you watch me sleep, too? [chuckles] 

245
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,295
Do you want me to be watching you?

246
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:57,341
Uh, no. Gross. I was just messing around.

247
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:00,636
Well, that's not the story
your heart rate is telling.

248
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:04,557
I'm going into battle tomorrow.

249
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:09,603
Anyway, um, I kind of thought
you were calling me

250
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:12,314
with an "I just want you to know."

251
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:13,482
A what?

252
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,735
You know, an "I just want you to know."

253
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:19,321
It's like when people are like,
"If we never see each other again,

254
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:21,115
I just want you to know,

255
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:24,535
like, how I feel."

256
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:27,955
[clears throat] Um...

257
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:30,958
You know that all communications
with the launch room

258
00:12:31,041 --> 00:12:33,461
are recorded for posterity, Captain?

259
00:12:35,212 --> 00:12:37,006
Okay. No. Copy that, Scientist.

260
00:12:37,089 --> 00:12:39,675
Yes, loud and clear, and never mind.

261
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:41,844
Actually, Chief Scientist now.

262
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:43,220
Dr. Mallory quit today.

263
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:45,389
Oh, wow. I mean...

264
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,641
Congratulations, I guess.

265
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:50,561
But I also can't help thinking
that means I'm fucked.

266
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,855
No. You're a superhero.

267
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,732
And the queen of TikTok.

268
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:56,609
The what?

269
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:58,736
[Angela's voice]
It's good to be black on the moon.

270
00:12:58,819 --> 00:12:59,695
Goddamn it.

271
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:01,697
[laughs] Okay.

272
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:05,910
I cannot believe that's only like
the tenth weirdest thing about today.

273
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:08,704
Thanks for showing me.

274
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:11,832
Yeah. Well, I just wanted you to know.

275
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,626
That I'm a meme?

276
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:16,712
Yeah! You know, in case, like,
we never see each other again,

277
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,881
I just wanted you to know.

278
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:27,181
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

279
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,770
Is there any, uh, sauce?

280
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,023
[sighing] 

281
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,650
I forgot the sauce.

282
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,318
Oh, that's no problem.

283
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:42,738
Do you have any cheese or, uh,
is there salad?

284
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,244
Mark, you said you were a good cook.

285
00:13:48,327 --> 00:13:49,161
Yeah.

286
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:51,622
I'm so sorry. I'm not gonna eat this.

287
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:53,916
I'm not two years old.

288
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,000
I apologize.

289
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:56,502
My focus is off.

290
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,921
-What's up?
-Adrian Mallory quit today.

291
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,799
Why? Did you make him dinner?

292
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:02,842
[sighs] 

293
00:14:03,634 --> 00:14:07,012
He didn't like something
that the military was doing.

294
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:09,807
Oh, well,
he sounds like a spoiled little shit.

295
00:14:10,307 --> 00:14:12,476
Sometimes he is, but not this time.

296
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:16,355
Well, will he come back
if you stop doing what you're doing?

297
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:18,941
Ah, I can't. It was an order.

298
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:22,528
No, what are you doing?

299
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:25,656
Mark, what are you--
No. Stop it. I cannot let you eat that.

300
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:26,574
It's barely cooked.

301
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:27,741
It's crunchy.

302
00:14:27,825 --> 00:14:28,951
Oh, God. Here.

303
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:29,952
[clears throat] 

304
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:31,745
No, no, no. No, no.

305
00:14:34,290 --> 00:14:38,043
I may be called upon to make a decision
that I have to be completely sober for.

306
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:41,213
It's not about sex, is it?
Cause I don't mind if you're tipsy.

307
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:43,507
[sighs]

308
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:48,762
I have to be prepared
to order soldiers into battle.

309
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:51,473
Can't really talk about it.

310
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:57,980
I don't know what to do.

311
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:02,359
[sighs]

312
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:05,696
When you asked me out,

313
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:08,699
you knew you had to tell me
about your wife.

314
00:15:09,199 --> 00:15:11,327
Even though it would probably ruin things.

315
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:14,622
You literally couldn't do the wrong thing.

316
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:17,249
So I'm not worried about you.

317
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:21,754
What if I don't know
what the right thing to do is?

318
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:26,508
But you do.

319
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,177
Don't you?

320
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:39,355
Help me defy an order.

321
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,027
Ooh.

322
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,656
That is where I shine.

323
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:52,534
I've been defying authority
since I was 13.

324
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:57,873
And now I'm gonna teach you

325
00:15:57,957 --> 00:16:00,918
to use the most subversive weapon
known to man:

326
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,127
passive-aggression.

327
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,504
Oh, God, I hate that.

328
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:04,463
Yeah, of course,

329
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:08,217
because you're a straight white male,
you always had other weapons.

330
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:12,096
But the rest of us,
we have to be subtle in our disobedience,

331
00:16:12,179 --> 00:16:13,305
or we risk punishment.

332
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,724
Oh, so interesting.
Go on. I'm so interested.

333
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:18,519
No, see, that's sarcasm. That's different.

334
00:16:18,852 --> 00:16:20,771
Imagine in this situation,

335
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:24,233
you could say that
you're following through with the order,

336
00:16:24,316 --> 00:16:25,984
but then you forget to,

337
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:28,862
or you can interpret
that order creatively.

338
00:16:28,946 --> 00:16:31,615
"Destroy the bathroom"
could mean a number of things

339
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:35,202
and, if all else fails,
you can feign incompetent,

340
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:36,578
which shouldn't be a problem.

341
00:16:36,662 --> 00:16:38,539
Well, that explains Brad, doesn't it?

342
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:39,915
Not entirely.

343
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,250
Huh. 

344
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:44,962
[ringing]

345
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,840
-What are we to do?
-I'll handle it!

346
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:48,924
He'll handle it.

347
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:52,970
Mr. Secretary, I just want to let you know
before we begin,

348
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:55,723
that I am running low on cell battery,
so I may lose you.

349
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:57,850
Uh, here's the situation as it stands.

350
00:16:58,684 --> 00:16:59,560
Well done, sir.

351
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,895
Nobody answer the phone
for the next two hours.

352
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:02,938
Yes, sir.

353
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:10,112
[Mark] Oh, my God. Oh, my God!

354
00:17:10,487 --> 00:17:12,906
[groaning] Oh, shit! Oh, shit. 

355
00:17:21,123 --> 00:17:21,957
Got a smoke?

356
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:26,670
Can't buy your own?

357
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:28,172
I can.

358
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:30,507
Just don't feel like it.

359
00:17:30,924 --> 00:17:31,884
[scoffs]

360
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:38,140
Tell you what.

361
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:40,392
I'll give it to you in my truck.

362
00:17:46,106 --> 00:17:47,816
Come on. We're going to a party.

363
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,615
Fuck it.

364
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:20,682
[Mallory] I've got it.

365
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:24,436
Beijing is hosting
the Winter Olympics 2022.

366
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,437
We boycott.

367
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:26,814
Then they win even more medals.

368
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:29,775
No, China's surprisingly awful
at Winter Olympic sports.

369
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:31,777
But boy-oh-boy, Norway would be happy.

370
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,821
Okay, say you are a criminal.

371
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:36,615
What would be meaner
than TP-ing somebody's house,

372
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:39,660
but not as aggressive
as home invasion-slash-murder?

373
00:18:39,743 --> 00:18:42,412
Tying the family up and letting them think
they're gonna be murdered.

374
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,748
Then they live
with the fear and horror forever.

375
00:18:45,749 --> 00:18:48,544
Jesus, Brad.
No wonder my dogs are scared of you.

376
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:49,545
[knocking on door]

377
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:52,422
Uh, excuse me, General, sir.

378
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,800
The Sec Def is on
in the conference room for you.

379
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:56,969
Balls!

380
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,346
All right, tell him I'll be right there.

381
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:00,472
Put him on hold.

382
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,559
-What are you gonna say?
-I'm not gonna say anything.

383
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:06,145
I'm gonna go eat egg salad sandwiches
until I puke.

384
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:18,448
Uh...

385
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:21,743
Hey. Hey!

386
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,580
Hey, I think, um, you can just let me out,
like, right here.

387
00:19:24,663 --> 00:19:26,540
That's-- That's totally fine.

388
00:19:28,917 --> 00:19:30,419
Hey. You guys.

389
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,046
Hey! Let me out here, okay?

390
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:36,008
Excuse me!

391
00:19:36,758 --> 00:19:38,552
Can you please let me out?

392
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:41,597
Fucking kidding me!

393
00:19:45,809 --> 00:19:48,562
What the hell?
Did you guys not hear me yelling?

394
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,450
[sighs]

395
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:10,334
They're stonewalling us.

396
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:12,294
Where-- Where-- Where's Grabaston?

397
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:14,046
[Kick] In the air 
and ready to swoop in!

398
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:17,716
Big Eagle is ready to replace
the Dodo Bird!

399
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:19,843
[Mark] I like what you said up there.

400
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:21,803
I wish I was black on the moon.

401
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:23,555
Thank you, sir.

402
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:27,434
Captain, when we first met,
you disobeyed an order.

403
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:30,896
Yeah, I remember it well, sir.

404
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,357
Today, I'm thinking about doing the same.

405
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,027
This is being recorded, General.

406
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:45,410
The generation that won World War II
was exposed to so much awful reality

407
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:50,332
that they made mostly good decisions
for a long time after.

408
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:56,171
Forget history, and you are doomed
to repeat the mistakes of the past.

409
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:58,715
Forget how bad polio was,

410
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:00,968
people stop taking vaccines.

411
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:04,263
Forget how bad world wars are,

412
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,390
people start puffing out their chests.

413
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,851
The real enemy is arrogance.

414
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:18,193
Angela, I think there are springs
and bolts and such

415
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:20,404
in those Manchester Arms devices

416
00:21:20,487 --> 00:21:22,948
that would be better used
to build your habitat.

417
00:21:23,031 --> 00:21:26,702
I'd like you to disassemble them
and let Eddie use the parts.

418
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:29,997
You're telling me to... [clears throat]

419
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:32,708
...to take the guns apart,
which would disable them, General.

420
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:33,834
That is correct.

421
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:38,171
Thin ice, General.

422
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:40,257
Thin ice.

423
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:58,650
[clears throat] 

424
00:21:58,734 --> 00:21:59,693
ID?

425
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:02,779
Step aside, Gomer.

426
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:07,784
Sir, I need to see some Space Force ID
to let anyone inside.

427
00:22:08,201 --> 00:22:10,120
Here is my Space Force ID.

428
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:12,914
[whooshing]

429
00:22:13,957 --> 00:22:15,292
[imitates explosion]

430
00:22:17,377 --> 00:22:19,588
And a second ID with a photo.

431
00:22:19,921 --> 00:22:20,881
[stammers] 

432
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:23,258
A passport, Costco card.

433
00:22:24,009 --> 00:22:25,260
If you have to run on home--

434
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:26,803
Oh, for fuck's sakes, restrain him.

435
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:27,763
Gladly.

436
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:37,230
General Naird!

437
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:42,402
You were ordered to order an attack,
and I am ordering you to obey that order.

438
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:44,029
I'm not your waitress, Kick.

439
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:46,615
I'm going to count to 125.

440
00:22:46,698 --> 00:22:47,949
Just count to three.

441
00:22:48,033 --> 00:22:51,411
Counting to 125 will give you ample time
to think it over.

442
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:52,788
This is wrong, Kick.

443
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,790
Deep down, you know it, too.

444
00:22:54,873 --> 00:22:56,458
I don't give a shit.

445
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:58,085
Arrest him.

446
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:03,131
And don't try to run, Naird,
or we'll shoot you in the back.

447
00:23:06,134 --> 00:23:08,136
Get me whoever is in charge up there.

448
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,971
Her name is Captain Ali, sir.

449
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:14,684
Captain Ali, you are hereby ordered
to attack the Chinese base.

450
00:23:14,768 --> 00:23:15,727
Can't, sir.

451
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:16,728
Guns are disabled.

452
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:20,107
The barrels are now water pipes,
and the springs are in the thermostats.

453
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:22,901
Naird... that's treason.

454
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:25,612
It's not treason
to disobey an unlawful order.

455
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:29,241
Well, there must be something else
you can use as weapons.

456
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,743
We have a crazy amount of wrenches.

457
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:34,663
The big brainiac
packed wrench after wrench.

458
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:35,705
Go get 'em.

459
00:23:36,081 --> 00:23:37,207
Bigger the better.

460
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:39,334
Sir, where is General Naird?

461
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:41,002
I am in command now.

462
00:23:41,628 --> 00:23:43,505
It's wrenchin' time.

463
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:48,093
It, um... It looks like
we're actually doing this.

464
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:50,428
[clears throat] Everybody suit up.

465
00:23:51,138 --> 00:23:52,055
Boots on the moon.

466
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,558
Boots on the moon.

467
00:23:57,352 --> 00:23:58,311
[exhales] 

468
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:01,189
Julio!

469
00:24:02,023 --> 00:24:04,109
-Spacesuit.
-Oh. Yes.

470
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:47,152
Oh, okay.

471
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:49,487
[cell phone buzzing] 

472
00:24:58,038 --> 00:24:59,998
[whispering] 
Hey, Bug, it's not really a good time.

473
00:25:00,081 --> 00:25:03,627
Dad, Dad, I'm in the desert, west of town,
with some sketchy dudes.

474
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:04,586
[groans] 

475
00:25:04,669 --> 00:25:07,297
Erin, it doesn't sound like
you're making good choices.

476
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:08,924
You have to make good choices.

477
00:25:09,007 --> 00:25:12,093
It wasn't. It was a terrible choice,
but I need you to come get me, okay?

478
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:14,221
You said I could always call you
if I needed a ride.

479
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:17,432
I know, I know I did.
But I can't come right now.

480
00:25:17,515 --> 00:25:18,600
I've been arrested.

481
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:20,977
What? No. Mom was arrested.

482
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,312
Yeah, I'm aware of that.

483
00:25:22,395 --> 00:25:24,439
I'm... I have been, too. I'm sorry.

484
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,524
Well, that's great!

485
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:29,236
Both my parents are in jail,
and I can't get a tattoo. Okay.

486
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,278
Honey! Honey! 

487
00:25:30,695 --> 00:25:31,571
God.

488
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:33,657
Fu...

489
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:36,326
All right.

490
00:25:36,409 --> 00:25:38,954
[cell phone buzzing] 

491
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:41,623
Yeah.

492
00:25:45,293 --> 00:25:47,170
[Erin] Duncan, it's Erin. 
Can you come get me?

493
00:25:47,254 --> 00:25:49,422
No. I'm sitting next to your dad.

494
00:25:49,881 --> 00:25:51,049
I got arrested, too.

495
00:25:51,132 --> 00:25:51,967
[Erin] Fuck!

496
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,468
[line disconnects]

497
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:22,581
For the record, I am against this action.

498
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:23,873
Someone's taking notes, right?

499
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:27,252
This is all Kick's baby now.

500
00:26:31,131 --> 00:26:32,465
We can't let this happen.

501
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:34,050
Fuck Tony, come with me.

502
00:26:36,678 --> 00:26:38,597
My name is Dr. Adrian Mallory.

503
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:42,684
I am the former Chief Scientist
of Space Force.

504
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:46,521
And if the world
does not stop this madness,

505
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:49,441
I will set myself on fire!

506
00:26:49,524 --> 00:26:51,359
Yes, the entire world is listening.
This is your moment.

507
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:55,780
